It's an artifact of nethack pre-3.3.0 (or was that pre-3.2.0?), when
there were no races and Elf was a class.  Then, there was no reason
not to genocide h, as you were never an h, always an @.  Now, if you
play a gnome, dwarf, or orc (race), you are represented by an @ unless
you use the showrace option (which isn't that bad of an idea).

The point is that elves have always been @, dwarves h, gnomes G and
orcs o.  When you play one, you just see @ for historical reasons
unless you use showrace option.  Then, it's more obvious.  It's just a
bigger problem when playing a dwarf, since they share the same letter
as some really nasty, genocide-worthy monsters (there are no really
nasty G or o monsters IMO).

TDT made a conscious decision that genociding a class to which your
character belongs should still work, just like genociding all @ was
always a bad thing (up until 3.3.0 when you (@) weren't necessarily an
@).

